From: Ryan Qin <ryqin@google.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:26:43 -0800
Subject: [FedCM] Return early in RedirectTo() if the navigation destroys it

RequestHandler::RedirectTo() navigates the RP's frame and then completes
the request. The navigation can synchronously destroy the RP frame, and
with it this RequestHandler, which was then used afterwards. Return
early if that happens.

Fixed: 576991116
Change-Id: I556734e3d564cf4feafeba7f859727041992d5f4
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8753440
Reviewed-by: Yi Gu <yigu@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Ryan Qin <ryqin@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1739256}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
On this branch the request handling lives in RequestService
(content/browser/webid/request_service.cc) rather than RequestHandler; the
weak-pointer guard is applied to RequestService::RedirectTo().
request_handler_unittest.cc does not exist here; the test was not carried.

diff --git a/content/browser/webid/request_service.cc b/content/browser/webid/request_service.cc
index a796da57ceb8cfec993f178f49d72fefe0bbf2c3..1e46f5f7c1d32b30893a4e5951e26a07de265630 100644
--- a/content/browser/webid/request_service.cc
+++ b/content/browser/webid/request_service.cc
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include "base/json/json_reader.h"
 #include "base/json/json_writer.h"
 #include "base/memory/scoped_refptr.h"
+#include "base/memory/weak_ptr.h"
 #include "base/metrics/histogram_macros.h"
 #include "base/rand_util.h"
 #include "base/strings/escape.h"
@@ -1906,7 +1907,12 @@ void RequestService::RedirectTo(const GURL& idp_config_url,
         "Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\r\n";
   }
   in_redirect_to_ = true;
+  // The navigation can synchronously destroy `this`.
+  base::WeakPtr<RequestService> weak_this = weak_ptr_factory_.GetWeakPtr();
   web_contents->GetController().LoadURLWithParams(params);
+  if (!weak_this) {
+    return;
+  }
 
   CompleteRequest(FederatedAuthRequestResult::kSuccess,
                   TokenStatus::kSuccessUsingRedirectTo,
